  "result": "The O3 lesson, its quiz and a cheat sheet are written; I'm just wrapping up.\n\n- **Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory.html`, set to 30 minutes for O3. I didn't run a word count, so my estimate is about 3,800 words, inside the 2,700–6,750 range that counts as fitting.\n- **What it covers:**\n  - The context window and tokens.\n  - What carries between steps, with a cost worked example, since every call resends the whole history.\n  - Context rot, tool-result clearing and compaction.\n  - Notes as memory between sessions.\n  - Retrieval: chunking, embeddings and keyword search for exact codes.\n  - A table that maps each symptom to the move that fixes it.\n  - A worked example on the laser cutter, then a token-cost exercise for you to do.\n- **Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json` has five items, with its key in `keys/0002.json`. It's ready when you are; I haven't shown you any answers.\n- **Cheat sheet:** `cheatsheets/context-and-memory.html`. I also updated `RESOURCES.md` and `NOTES.md`.\n- **Sources:** I read three Anthropic pages in full: the context-engineering post, the context-windows doc and the contextual-retrieval post. I cited only URLs from this session's search results.\n- **Not done:**\n  - Quiz 0001 is still ungraded; I only noted that in `NOTES.md`.\n  - I found no verified community for agent builders, so the lesson says so instead of inventing one.\n\nAsk me anything in the chat if a section is unclear. Do you want me to look for a community to add?",
